      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page (called [[write-journal]]) describes how the guarded write path in Grimoire manages file changes with rollback capability:\n\n**Key points:**\n\n1. **Pre-write recording**: Before overwriting any file, the guarded tool executor records the file\u0027s prior state \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or a record that it did not exist \u2014 in an in-memory write journal.\n\n2. **Rollback on failure**: If the agent run fails (due to turn cap exceeded, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can reverse all recorded writes in reverse order: restoring previous content for existing files and deleting newly created files.\n\n3. **All-or-nothing semantics**: This approach provides atomic transaction-like behavior for the agent\u0027s writes without needing a database \u2014 the journal itself serves as the transaction log, held only in the process\u0027s memory during a single run.\n\n4. **Query agent note**: The Query agent (which this Grimoire wiki uses) doesn\u0027t utilize the rollback functionality since it has no write tool; the journal exists in the shared runtime library but is only populated by agents that actually write.",
      "input_tokens": 4318,
